{
 "schema": "semio.os-dev.interaction-latency-scenarios/v1",
 "description": "Interactions the latency gate drives in the served s shell: the input, its target and the bounds the measurement is judged by. Input → end of the first frame after it; paints = renderFrame calls of the canvas session classes (wasm bindings and host elements) during the gesture; a scenario whose paints could not be hooked fails. Commits = React root commits of every renderer (react-dom, r3f) per input, counted through a minimal DevTools global hook; hover = the pointer alternately onto a point whose hover the target paints into hoverAttribute, and off it. A highlighted editor (trinity jack) paints each key twice by design — the local edit, then the guest's re-highlighted echo — plus the caret cadence (2 per second) inside the measured window.",
 "loadCeilingPerCore": 1.0,
